From: our reconstruction of GL.iNet's 4.6.x-4.8.2 MPTCP backport
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: subflow_v4_init_req as GL.iNet's stub

GL.iNet's kernels 4.6.2 to 4.8.2 have subflow_v4_init_req() as a stub: it
sets is_mptcp and prints "MPTCP: mptcp need to implement this function"
with __FILE__, __func__ and __LINE__ (1791); their later published backport
(ours) implements it. Compiled the validated way, this gives GL.iNet's
14 instructions exactly (line 1791 included).

---
--- a/net/mptcp/subflow.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
@@ -1788,8 +1788,7 @@
 				struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	tcp_rsk(req)->is_mptcp = 1;
-	tcp_request_sock_ipv4_ops.init_req(req, sk_listener, skb);
-	subflow_init_req(req, sk_listener);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "MPTCP: mptcp need to implement this function: %s,%s,%d", __FILE__, __func__, __LINE__);
 }
 
 void __init mptcp_subflow_init(void)
